PCA(Principal Component Analysis)

It Comes under pre-process
It is nothing but the process of reducing dimension(column) to low dimension data
eg:From 10 columns it will create a 3 new column
PCA works only with numeric columns

Note:
To reduce no of features

Q/A
1.Why we should reduce dimension?
 1.1 This is to solve  the problem of "Curse of dimensionality ."
 1.2 This is t0 address  multi collinearity(when columns are highly correlated to each other)
 So PCA creates uncorrelated features.
  eg:
     If columns,like "house_price","No of bed rooms","no of rest room" is part of
     your input  data then it is called multi collinearity.

2.How PCA works?
  Step 1:
        House_price will be in rupees,no of bed rooms,no of rest room will in single digit integer.
        So all three input will be in different scale,So we have to standardize or normalize it.

  Note:
       If you don't standardize housing price will take higher variance.
  Step2:
       Each of the column("house_price","No of bed rooms","no of rest room" ) will be transformed to have mean
       avg of 0 under std deviation of 1.
